(    1) MODULE YOE_CUCONVCA
(    2) 
(    3) ! Modified : 
(    4) !    R. El Khatib 09-Mar-2012 Allocate RCUCONVCA/RNLCONVCA for safe bound checkings later
(    5) !    L. Bengtsson 05-Aug-2014 Correction if using with GOL
(    6) !    L. Gerard    31-Mar-2016 Add RCADELX
(    7) USE PARKIND1 , ONLY : JPIM, JPRB
(    8) 
(    9) IMPLICIT NONE
(   10) 
(   11) SAVE
(   12) 
(   13) !     ------------------------------------------------------
(   14) 
(   15) !*    control parameters for cellular automaton for convection
(   16) 
(   17) !      yd_random_stream_CA: random number stream for CA update
(   18) !      NIJH         : Multiplicative for number of points in high resolution grid
(   19) !      NBmax        : maximum possible number of neighbours for every gridcell
(   20) !      RCADELX      : Length of individual CA cell (meters) to compute NIJH
(   21) !      RCUCONVCA    : Array for interaction with the physics
(   22) !      RNLCONVCA    : Array for interaction with the physics
(   23) !      RCAPECONVCA  : Array to store "good" CAPE between its calculation [MOD(KSTEP*TSPHY,3600._JPRB)]
(   24) !      NCELLCU      : Lat-lon grid for cellular automaton
(   25) !      NFERTCU      : Lat-lon grid for cellular automaton (fertile cell indicator)
(   26) !      NBLS         : neighbours for large scale grid (= model red gaussian grid)
(   27) !      NBSS         : neighbours for small scale grid (= NIJH*NIJH cells in every LS cell)
(   28) !      NRNBLS       : number of neighbours for large scale cells
(   29) !      NRNBSS       : number of neighbours for small scale cells
(   30) !      NBNS         : neighbour north/south or on same lat (1/-1/0)
(   31) !      NBEW         : neighbour east/west or on same long (1/-1/0)
(   32) !      RWASALIVE    : Array indicating grid-points where CA was alive before
(   33) !      RWGHTCU      : Weighted and smoothed CA pattern
(   34) !      LCUCONV_CA   : TRUE IF CELLULAR AUTOMATON USED IN CONVECTION
(   35) !      LCA_ADVECT   : switch for "kind of" semi-Lagrangian advection
(   36) !      LCA_GLOBAL   : switch for global CA instead ov "convective" CA
(   37) !      LCA_SMOOTH   : swith for smoothing CA on large scale grid
(   38) !      LCA_RANTROP  : switch for random coupling of CA to deep convection (concerns initialization)
(   39) !      LCA_TEST     : switch for initialize CA at single point
(   40) !      LCA_ADVTEST  : switch for advection test (CA only evolved first 5 steps)
(   41) !      NTESTPROC    : set on which processor the single point should lie
(   42) !      NTESTGP      : set which gridpoint the single point is on
(   43) !      NSPINUP      : set number of spin-up cycles for global pattern
(   44) !      CA_FORC      : switch to choose convective forcing
(   45) !      CA_WIND      : switch to choose CA-wind (real/idealized)
(   46) !      CA_PROB      : switch to choose probabilities
(   47) !      NLIVES       : switch to choose number of lives (scaled by CAPE in callpar)
(   48) !      NFERTYRS     : switch to choose max number of steps a cell can be fertile
(   49) !      NFRCASEED    : Frequency of seeding CA where physics diagnoses deep convection
(   50) !      RCA_SEEDPROB : Probability of random seeding for global CA






NVFORTRAN (Version     24.5)          03/19/2025  06:54:21      page 2

(   51) 
(   52) !      RPROB_SURVIVE: probabilities for cell survival
(   53) !      RPROB_BIRTH: probabilities for cell birth
(   54) !      RPROB_FUN_FERT_S: function for specifying probabilities for survival as function of upwind(uw)+downwind(dw) neighbour
(   55) !      RPROB_FUN_UW_DW_S: function for specifying probabilities for survival as function of upwind(uw)-downwind(dw) neighbou
(   56) !      RPROB_FUN_FERT_B: function for specifying probabilities for birth as function of upwind(uw)+downwind(dw) neighbours
(   57) !      RPROB_FUN_UW_DW_B: function for specifying probabilities for birth as function of upwind(uw)-downwind(dw) neighbours
(   58) 
(   59) !      SLLONG(YRSL%NASLB1)       : Array containing the longitude for each gridpoint in a semi/lagrangian buffer array
(   60) !      SLLAT(YRSL%NASLB1)        : Array containing the latitude for each gridpoint in a semi/lagrangian buffer array
(   61) !      SLDLONG(YRSL%NASLB1)      : Array containing the width of each gridbox in longitudinal direction 
